WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:06.319
Future film foreshadowing, environmental rage,
and a red herring that caught us all off-guard.

00:00:06.319 --> 00:00:10.010
These brief lines in "Avatar: The Way of Water"
hold an ocean of depth.

00:00:10.729 --> 00:00:16.458
Both "Avatar" films have a similar framing
device: they begin and end with Jake Sully's narration.

00:00:16.458 --> 00:00:21.929
In the prologue of "Way of Water," Jake waxes
poetic about his beautiful wife and beloved children.

00:00:21.929 --> 00:00:27.060
Besides Neytiri, his family has grown to include
adopted daughter Kiri, oldest son Neteyam,

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:30.340
youngest son Lo'ak, and youngest daughter
Tuk.

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:34.880
Viewers get the sense that, after the traumatic
destruction of Hometree, nature and the Na'vi

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:36.250
people are healing together.

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:37.250
But then he warns —

00:00:42.539 --> 00:00:47.559
By this, he means his family, the Na'vi community
that's taken him in, and the natural beauty

00:00:47.559 --> 00:00:50.470
and scientific wonder of the moon they all
live on.

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:54.550
Jake often tells Neytiri that he loves her
in conjunction with her people and their world.

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:59.590
It makes sense that he speaks this way; the
Na'vi know that everything on Pandora is connected.

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:04.400
His fear of losing his happiness is a fear
of losing his family, his clan, and his new

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:05.400
home world.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.340
So when Jake's monologue ends with the line
—

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:16.250
— he's referring to his own as well as that
of everyone he loves — including Eywa, the

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:16.929
Great Mother.

00:01:16.929 --> 00:01:19.178
"What does Eywa's heartbeat sound like?"

00:01:19.178 --> 00:01:20.178
"Mighty."

00:01:20.178 --> 00:01:25.320
The quote is tragic foreshadowing, indicating
that someone's heartbeat is soon to stop.

00:01:25.798 --> 00:01:29.630
In his opening monologue, Jake catches the
audience up to speed on what he and the rest

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:32.320
of the Sully clan have been up to for the
last decade and a half.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:36.360
The audience sees him welcoming his children
into the world, teaching them how to hunt

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:40.180
and fish, and accompanying Neytiri on a twilight
banshee-ride date night.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:44.640
As Jake describes each milestone in English,
the rest of the Na'vi communicate with one

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:48.700
another using the language Cameron and a linguist
invented for the franchise.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:52.049
Jake jokes about how long it took him to speak
the language fluently.

00:01:52.049 --> 00:01:54.009
He concludes by saying that, now,

00:01:55.810 --> 00:02:00.600
In that moment, Jake's family's dialogue switches
to English, even though the audience is meant

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:03.210
to understand that they're all speaking Na'vi.

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:07.700
This is a slick screenwriting trick, a way
to acknowledge and preserve Pandora's on-screen

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:12.450
culture without making the actors do the entirety
of their performance in a fictional language.

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:16.671
The remainder of "Avatar: The Way of Water"
is spoken almost entirely in English, except

00:02:16.671 --> 00:02:20.261
for moments where what's lost in translation
is part of the plot.

00:02:20.748 --> 00:02:25.530
Jake admits that, although he and his kids
love Spider — a feral boy left behind by

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:30.080
the humans — Neytiri struggles to see him
as anything but an outsider and a threat.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:33.380
At the beginning, the audience doesn't know
if she's aware of the truth about his parentage,

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:37.430
but by the end, it's clear that some of her
hesitation about accepting the boy into their

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:40.630
family has to do with the fact that he's Quaritch's
son.

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:44.379
It was Neytiri who dealt the depraved Colonel
a fatal blow with her father's bow and arrow

00:02:44.379 --> 00:02:48.879
at the end of the original "Avatar," which
we see play out again on the mech suit camera.

00:02:48.879 --> 00:02:53.246
Years later, Recombinant Quaritch lands on
Pandora to seek revenge on the traitor Jake Sully.

00:02:53.246 --> 00:02:58.010
He essentially lucks into kidnapping the Sully
kids at the site of the old mobile lab, discovers

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:02.500
Neytiri was responsible for his death, and
is nearly able to take her out...

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:04.220
all in the same scene.

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:08.380
Before his plan is interrupted, he shouts
in her direction that he recognizes her call

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:10.920
sign: the color of the fletches on her arrows.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:14.579
She recognizes his voice, and though she's
confused, yells back —

00:03:17.429 --> 00:03:21.420
At the end of the film, Jake and Neytiri think
Recombinant Quaritch is at the bottom of the

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:25.610
ocean — but since Spider couldn't bring
himself to let him die, he'll most certainly

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:26.990
be back in "Avatar 3."

00:03:27.689 --> 00:03:33.170
There's a great deal of talk about the life
cycle in "Way of Water," and it begins long

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:35.360
before the Sullys get to the reef.

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:39.600
After their encounter with Recombinant Quaritch,
Jake realizes the humans are specifically

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:44.250
targeting his family and decides the best
course of action — for the Sullys and for

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:46.519
the Omaticaya — is for them to leave.

00:03:46.519 --> 00:03:49.819
This is easier said than done: he's the clan
leader.

00:03:49.819 --> 00:03:53.860
According to their traditions, the old leader
must die before the new one can assume his

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:57.650
place — something Jake learned firsthand
all those years ago.

00:03:57.970 --> 00:03:59.329
"I will not kill you."

00:03:59.771 --> 00:04:01.128
"It is the way!

00:04:03.197 --> 00:04:04.759
And it is good."

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:11.120
Tarsem, the incoming Omaticaya leader, ceremonially
slashes Jake across the chest and says,

00:04:13.669 --> 00:04:17.410
With that, the Sully family takes to their
banshees for parts unknown.

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:22.000
Throughout the film, there are a number of
hints that Jake may meet his untimely end,

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:25.700
and this reference to his own symbolic death
is just one of them.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:30.250
Jake frequently talks about protecting his
family at all costs, which primes viewers

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:34.840
to think he's going to make the ultimate sacrifice
when it comes down to it, to save his children

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:36.220
and his people.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:40.790
That's exactly what the plot sets up in its
third act: Quaritch has Jake's kids captive

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:44.539
on the Sea Dragon, and he's only willing to
exchange them for Jake's life.

00:04:44.539 --> 00:04:48.040
Of course, the emphasis on Jake's mortality
is a red herring.

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:52.490
Tragically, it's Jake and Neytiri's oldest
son, Neteyam, who doesn't survive the battle.

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:53.490
They will be like babies

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:57.600
When the Sullys arrive safely at the reef,
Jake feels relatively confident that the Metkayina

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:02.360
people will grant them shelter — after all,
he was the great Turok Makto until very recently.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:07.380
Tonowari, the leader of the Metkayina, knows
of his legend and is welcoming, but is also

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:10.470
concerned about the possibility of war coming
to his shores.

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:14.639
His wife and the clan's medicine woman, Ronal,
is much more skeptical.

00:05:14.639 --> 00:05:18.530
She correctly deduces that the Sullys had
to leave High Camp because they posed a problem

00:05:18.530 --> 00:05:22.060
to the Omaticaya, and she doesn't want to
bother teaching her ways to people who won't

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:23.730
be receptive or capable.

00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:24.891
She tells Tonowari —

00:05:26.829 --> 00:05:30.316
This line is a callback to when Jake and Neytiri
meet in the first "Avatar."

00:05:30.316 --> 00:05:32.487
"You're like a baby."

00:05:35.359 --> 00:05:40.830
What Neytiri means is that Jake was loud,
clumsy, and unaware of his impact on the world

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:41.830
around him.

00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:45.750
When her mother charged her with teaching
Jake the ways of the Na'vi, she bristled,

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:48.360
reasoning that they'd essentially have to
start from scratch.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:50.470
Now, the tables are turned.

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:55.720
While Ronal's daughter, Tsireya, is noticeably
more up for the challenge, Ronal still asserts

00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:59.330
that it won't be easy for the forest Na'vi
to fit in at the reef.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:03.789
Her comment is both a statement of prejudice
and a reasonable attempt at isolating her

00:06:03.789 --> 00:06:05.160
clan from danger...

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:08.521
two themes seen consistently throughout the
"Avatar" series.

00:06:08.919 --> 00:06:13.199
The flip side of Ronal's line is Jake's answer
to it: he tells the Metkayina,

00:06:14.689 --> 00:06:17.340
Jake has adapted before, and he'll do it again.

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:22.300
He did it as a human after becoming paralyzed,
again when he was reborn as a Na'vi avatar,

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:26.960
and once more when he was finally accepted
into Na'vi society with a permanent, true

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:28.240
Na'vi body of his own.

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:33.060
Jake is also pointing out that, on a long
enough timeline, the Na'vi physically adapt.

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:36.710
Evolution has made the Na'vi distinct from
each other depending on the habitat in which

00:06:36.710 --> 00:06:41.569
they live: the Metkayina have evolved to have
lighter teal skin, thicker and flatter tails,

00:06:41.569 --> 00:06:44.940
muscular, almost finned wrists, and bigger
lungs.

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:49.460
They've adapted to their ecosystem, as will
the clans of Na'vi that audiences are likely

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:52.060
to meet in "Avatar 3" and beyond.

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:56.949
Given his circumstances, Jake is much less
prejudiced about physical differences than

00:06:56.949 --> 00:06:57.979
other Na'vi.

00:06:57.979 --> 00:07:03.009
The "Avatar" films are deeply interested in
the intersections between technology, biology,

00:07:03.009 --> 00:07:04.580
and environmental science.

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:10.030
Messages can be found throughout that not-so-discreetly
plead with humans to be better stewards of

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:13.240
their resources, their planet, and each other.

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:17.840
Cameron is challenging humans to evolve to
live within what Jake calls "the great balance"

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:21.031
rather than to continue old, destructive habits.

00:07:21.428 --> 00:07:25.550
If "Avatar: The Way of Water" has a thesis
statement, it's the words of the Metkayina

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:28.979
people — wisdom that Tsireya imparts to
a troubled Lo'ak.

00:07:28.979 --> 00:07:29.798
She tells him —

00:07:36.679 --> 00:07:41.169
She goes on to compare water to a womb that
births us into a world which exists before

00:07:41.169 --> 00:07:43.669
we're here and remains after we die.

00:07:43.669 --> 00:07:48.560
It's a moving speech, made even more lovely
by the actor's calm, contemplative delivery,

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:51.580
and the entrancing shots of Pandora's marine
wildlife.

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:53.610
"Alien, that's all they see!"

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:57.270
Tsireya's lesson is meant to make Lo'ak feel
as though he's a part of something bigger

00:07:57.270 --> 00:07:58.759
than himself and his family.

00:07:58.759 --> 00:08:03.140
More broadly, it's meant to teach the forest-dwelling
Sullys about her clan's specific philosophy

00:08:03.140 --> 00:08:07.030
when it comes to the "great balance" that
Jake speaks of — the great balance that

00:08:07.030 --> 00:08:09.060
Earth's humans don't respect.

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:13.879
These Metkayina sentiments are religious in-world,
but they also represent the environmentally-conscious

00:08:13.879 --> 00:08:15.919
Cameron's personal philosophy.

00:08:15.919 --> 00:08:20.820
If that philosophy sounds strikingly similar
to the notion of the Force from "Star Wars"

00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:25.620
— especially as a more mature and slightly
jaded Luke Skywalker taught it to Rey in "The

00:08:25.620 --> 00:08:27.099
Last Jedi" — you're not alone.

00:08:27.099 --> 00:08:31.840
Both borrow from Eastern spiritual traditions
like Taoism and pantheistic religions that

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:32.840
revere nature.

00:08:33.177 --> 00:08:38.620
Pandora's sky is one of its most spectacular,
yet fraught features.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:43.469
Instead of days and nights with a sun followed
by a moon up above, this habitable moon has

00:08:43.469 --> 00:08:45.830
an enormous planet on its horizon.

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:50.630
It has nightly eclipses and some peculiar
seasons — but like any big rock floating

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:53.760
in space, its sky is full of stars.

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:57.550
Lo'ak, trying to make his father sound like
a hero for once, remarks:

00:08:59.209 --> 00:09:01.490
It's a touching moment… in theory.

00:09:01.490 --> 00:09:06.500
Lo'ak not only views his once-human father
as a true Na'vi, but that he's mythologized

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:10.730
his origin story to an extent that he'd probably
never actually admit.

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:14.950
But in the past 30 years, what appeared to
be falling stars turned out to be spacecraft

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:18.680
from Earth, sent mostly for nefarious purposes.

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:22.839
It's the white light of a ship burning its
way into Pandora's atmosphere that alerts

00:09:22.839 --> 00:09:26.600
Jake and Neytiri to the return of the humans
at the start of "The Way of Water."

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:27.850
"The humans are returning.

00:09:28.291 --> 00:09:29.420
They're hunting us."

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:33.840
And since the audience knows that Earth is
dying and humans have little choice but to

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:39.240
take over this distant moon by any means necessary,
it's not the last time these young Na'vi will

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:41.561
see an ominous star in Pandora's sky.

00:09:42.289 --> 00:09:47.160
Quaritch convinces his sort-of son, Spider,
to ride along on his squad's mission in order

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:49.130
to avoid the military's mental torture.

00:09:49.130 --> 00:09:54.500
He remains antagonistic to their efforts throughout
his captivity, making fun of their slow speed

00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:57.100
and poor understanding of the Na'vi language.

00:09:57.100 --> 00:10:02.260
He's a Tarzan-like teen among ten-foot-tall
blue Jarheads until he meets marine biologist

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:03.470
Dr. Ian Garvin.

00:10:03.470 --> 00:10:08.220
As heartless and hot-headed alphas Quaritch
and Captain Mick excitedly discuss the killing

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:12.790
and harvesting of tulkuns, a more subdued
and guilt-ridden Dr. Garvin walks through

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:15.030
each step of the operation with Spider.

00:10:15.030 --> 00:10:19.450
Once their target — the mother tulkun that
was Ronal's spirit sister — has been eliminated,

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:23.690
the hunting party ventures inside her corpse,
where a makeshift workspace has been set up.

00:10:23.690 --> 00:10:28.440
The team drills into the tulkun's brain, and
out comes a golden liquid... about enough

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:29.890
to fill a thermos.

00:10:29.890 --> 00:10:32.880
Captain Mick claims it is worth about $80
million.

00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:38.670
It turns out, Earth scientists have discovered
this substance has the power to stop human aging.

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:40.559
Spider has an issue with this, though.

00:10:40.559 --> 00:10:42.061
He asks, in rage —

00:10:44.299 --> 00:10:49.300
This is meant to show how irresponsible modern
industrialized humans are, compared to indigenous

00:10:49.300 --> 00:10:52.670
populations who live in harmony with their
natural resources.

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:58.320
The whaling operation's wastefulness is even
more horrific once the film explains how acutely

00:10:58.320 --> 00:11:00.591
tulkuns are able to think and feel.

